  "name": "The Crooked Tree",
  "region": "crooked_tree",
  "summary": "A flat glade of short green-grey grass in bright moonlight, a steep mound at its heart with a barren, impossibly twisted oak on it, and a goat skull at its foot.",
  "text": "The moon has never looked closer. It is huge and it is grinning. At the middle of the glade a mound heaves up, and on it stands the Crooked Tree: a bare, twisted oak forty feet to its first limb, its branches knotting themselves as you watch. A great goat skull lies at its base with a carved crescent tied between its horns, and under the trunk a narrow mouth glows the warm colour of a campfire. Embers rise from the grass toward the moon.",
